<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<chapter xml:id="chapter-hypothesis-setup" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Hypothesis Testing - Setup</title>

  <introduction>
    <p>
      Inferential statistics is fundamentally about hypothesis
      testing. A hypothesis is a claim about some conclusion, and the
      methods of hypothesis testing are ways of looking at the data to
      see if the conclusion is true. There are two chapter in this
      course devoted to hypothesis testing. In this first chapter, we
      have several outcomes that setup the backgrounds and methods.
      The chapter to follow will focus on actually implementing
      hypothesis testing for a variety of types of data. 
    </p>
  </introduction>

